    {
      "tag": "Grands",
      "h2": "Grandparents",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Le grand-pere</strong> = grandfather. <strong>La grand-mere</strong> = grandmother. Informal: <strong>Papi</strong> (grandad) and <strong>Mamie</strong> (granny).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Aunts",
      "h2": "Aunts & Uncles",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>L'oncle</strong> = uncle. <strong>La tante</strong> = aunt. Notice 'l'' is a shortened 'le' before a vowel (l'oncle).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Cousins",
      "h2": "Cousins",
      "body_html": "<p>Male cousin = <strong>le cousin</strong>. Female cousin = <strong>la cousine</strong>. Notice how French changes the spelling for gender — many nouns work this way.</p>"
    }
  ],
